    {
      "id": "Ugx60jd-Ct5KgVFXEfp4AaABAg",
      "author": "@richardleighton5009",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_mDv2TpGcUKI5fpN6yMl2RQ-5vjAL5HEy0QcyoIN_Y=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Gold can be found in the mountains, rivers, and streams of Tajikistan. The country is rich in mineral resources, including gold, with significant deposits located in various regions. Placer mining, which involves extracting gold from rivers and streams using techniques like sluicing, panning, and dredging, has historically been prominent due to the abundance of alluvial gold deposits in the area.\r\n Additionally, the Zarafshon River, known for its gold-bearing sands, highlights the potential for gold extraction in these waterways.\r\n Overall, Tajikistan has around 40 known gold deposits with a total estimated amount of about 500 tons.",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-18T23:24:00Z",
      "replyCount": 1,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "Ugx60jd-Ct5KgVFXEfp4AaABAg.A_fI98ONPIyA_fv-otDU73",
          "author": "@PlanetVista4K",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/UP1KuiI-ZYUr_V0QMZqUj3WrxSMAqB70paheckH8ptL_nqqbtqZa5KyGSVhQ0Mc9Ay6bF1Odbw=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "That's some incredible insight into Tajikistan's mineral wealth! It's fascinating to learn about the historical prominence of placer mining and the significant gold deposits.",
          "likeCount": 1,
          "publishedAt": "2026-08-19T05:12:15Z"
        }
      ]
    },
